    31	// Skeptic (Phase 4: the cross-family critic). An INDEPENDENT, fail-closed adversarial reviewer
    32	// that challenges the pipeline's finding BEFORE it is accepted to ACT. It sits after the
    33	// deterministic findings (Sentinel -> Verifier -> Atlas -> Simulator) and BEFORE the act/refuse
    34	// gate (decideRecommendation). Its verdict gates STRENGTH-AWARE (applySkepticGate below, the
    35	// 2026-06-28 false-veto fix): a non-accept HARD-VETOES (forces NO_ACTION) unless the finding is
    36	// deterministically STRONG (corroborated + confidence >= floor + real exposure + no geo conflict),
    37	// in which case the objection DOWNGRADES to an ANNOTATED caution on the ACT packet -- the critic
    38	// informs, the deterministic evidence decides. An errored/broken critic always hard-vetoes.
    39	//
    40	// WHY a SECOND, CROSS-FAMILY model (ADR-0002): the self-preference bias -- a model rating its OWN
    41	// family's output more leniently -- is the most validated judge/critic bias (Panickssery, NeurIPS
    42	// 2024). The finding under review is Gemini's, so the Skeptic asks a DIFFERENT family (a non-Gemini
    43	// Groq model -- see lib/agents/cross-family.ts GROQ_DEFAULT_MODEL for the current id and the
    44	// 2026-07-27 L-1 re-point record) to try to knock it down. Its job is to catch what the
    45	// deterministic gates cannot: an OVER-TRIGGER (alert fatigue -- a scary headline that does not
    46	// actually threaten THIS buyer), a MISCLASSIFICATION, or THIN EVIDENCE (a lone uncorroborated
    47	// low-confidence source) -- and to REFUSE when it cannot stand behind acting.
    48	//
    49	// Two paths, mirroring the agent house pattern; the orchestrator (index.ts) routes per run:
    50	//   - runSkeptic (SYNC) is the DETERMINISTIC path, chosen for a non-live run. It returns an
    51	//     AFFIRMATIVE pass: the deterministic Verifier corroboration + decideRecommendation gate
    52	//     already screen the finding, so the Skeptic ADDS no gate when its live cross-family challenge
    53	//     is not running. Mode DETERMINISTIC_RULES, $0, PASS -- so the audit trail still gains a
    54	//     Skeptic run.
    55	//   - challengeFindingLive (ASYNC) is the LIVE cross-family path. Key-OFF (no Groq key + no
    56	//     injected generate) it short-circuits to the SAME affirmative pass with NO network. Key-ON it
    57	//     asks a non-Gemini model to adversarially challenge the finding and returns a FAIL-CLOSED
    58	//     verdict.
    59	//
    60	// FAIL-CLOSED (like the judge): a live call that was ATTEMPTED and BROKE (threw / unparseable /
    61	// budget breach) -> accepted:false (HOLD the finding), errored, mode FAILED_TO_FALLBACK. A broken
    62	// safety critic must REFUSE, never wave the finding through. NOTE the asymmetry with the other
    63	// agents: those degrade to their DETERMINISTIC OUTPUT; the Skeptic degrades to a HOLD, because the
    64	// whole point is that a critic that could not run cannot vouch for acting.
    65	//
    66	// QUARANTINE (load-bearing, Phase 2): the Skeptic must NOT inherit news-derived raw text. It is fed
    67	// ONLY the STRUCTURED finding (buildSkepticFinding) -- never threatCard.summary (Sentinel-derived
    68	// prose from raw articles) or an exposure rationale or a signal summary. Those would launder a
    69	// survived injection into a cross-family prompt. buildSkepticFinding omits all prose by
    70	// construction; evals/actionops-skeptic.test.ts proves it structurally.
    71	//
    72	// AUTHORITATIVE-BINDING: the verdict is a boolean GATE plus a free-text reason. NOTHING numeric is
    73	// ever bound from that reason -- the packet's Skeptic-hold missingEvidence item is TEMPLATED and
    74	// numeral-free (SKEPTIC_HOLD_EVIDENCE), and the critic's own words live only in the RUN-SKEPTIC
    75	// audit record, never restated as packet fact.
    76	
    77	// resolvedSkepticModel: the cross-family model id. SKEPTIC_MODEL overrides the shared Groq default.
    78	export function resolvedSkepticModel(): string {
    79	  return process.env.SKEPTIC_MODEL?.trim() || GROQ_DEFAULT_MODEL;
    80	}
