    82	// The Skeptic's output-token budget. COUNTER-INTUITIVE AND MEASURED (2026-07-27, L-1 follow-on):
    83	// Groq's rate limiter charges `input + max_completion_tokens` as RESERVED against the per-minute
    84	// window -- it does NOT bill actual output. The free-tier TPM ceiling for the gpt-oss models on
    85	// this key is 8,000 (read off a deliberate 413; identical for 120b and 20b, so switching model
    86	// size buys no headroom). The inherited 4,000 default therefore reserved 1,421 + 4,000 = 5,421
    87	// tokens for a call whose REAL output is ~360-370 tokens (reasoning included) -- over 11x what it
    88	// uses -- so a second call inside the same minute 429'd. Because the critic fails CLOSED, each
    89	// throttle became a HOLD, which the calibration then scored as a false REJECT: measured
    90	// TPR 100% / TNR 40%, with all six misses tagged "(error)", not bad judgement.
    91	//
    92	// Raising the budget makes it strictly WORSE (16,000 -> HTTP 413 "Request too large", a single
    93	// call exceeding the whole minute). Right-sizing DOWN is the fix: 1,200 keeps >3x headroom over
    94	// the measured ~370 while dropping the reservation to ~2,621, so ~3 calls/minute fit the window.
    95	// The prior 4,000 was safe only because llama-4-scout enjoyed a ~30K TPM allowance.
    96	//
    97	// If the Skeptic prompt grows materially, re-measure -- this constant is tied to the prompt size,
    98	// not a universal value. `npm run preflight:groq` checks availability, NOT throughput.
    99	//
   100	// SCOPE OF THE RESERVATION CLAIM (stated precisely rather than universally): the
   101	// input + max_completion_tokens accounting is EXACT on the 429/413 responses that report the
   102	// large figure -- 1,421 + 4,000 = 5,421 and 1,421 + 16,000 = 17,421 both match to the token
   103	// (gates/live-repair-2026-07-27/06-groq-429-413-root-cause.log). Other 429s in the same run
   104	// report a SMALLER `Requested` (~1,752-1,760) whose derivation we have not established, so the
   105	// rule is evidenced, not proven universal across every rejection path. What does NOT rest on the
   106	// mechanism: the fix DIRECTION is independently confirmed behaviourally -- the same calibration
   107	// went TNR 40% -> 100% as this budget came down and the harness spacing went up.
   108	export const SKEPTIC_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS = 1_200;
