Author:     Sharan Kumar <sharank98@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Mon Jul 27 15:24:38 2026 -0400
Commit:     Sharan Kumar <sharank98@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Mon Jul 27 15:24:38 2026 -0400

    fix(live): the cross-family Skeptic was DEAD — repoint + right-size + preflight + teeth
    
    The live agentic product produced NOTHING. A first-hand full-loop smoke on the REAL path
    (no injected Skeptic) returned effectiveMode=FAILED_TO_FALLBACK, recommendation=NO_ACTION,
    gatekeeper BLOCKED, 0 playbooks, 0 drafts.
    
    L-1 [CRITICAL] — `meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct` was DECOMMISSIONED by Groq
    (absent from the key's ListModels). The Skeptic fails CLOSED, so the outage presented as
    silence and could never alarm on itself. The same shared constant also took down
    lib/evals/judge.ts. Nothing caught it: the preflight covered Gemini only, the gated live
    suite injects a stub ACCEPT Skeptic, and zero tests referenced the model id.
    
    L-2 [HIGH] — repointing alone was not enough. Groq reserves `input + max_completion_tokens`
    against an 8,000 TPM free-tier window, so the inherited maxOutputTokens 4_000 reserved
    ~5,421 tokens for a call that really emits ~370 → 429 → HOLD. Raising it is strictly worse
    (16k → HTTP 413). Sized DOWN to 1,200. The calibration harness's 4s spacing carried the same
    stale 30K-TPM assumption and was measuring its own throttling, not the critic's judgement.
    
    Changes
    - cross-family.ts: GROQ_DEFAULT_MODEL -> openai/gpt-oss-120b, chosen by LIVE probe through the
      real generate+schema path (only 2 of 4 candidates support json_schema; llama-3.3-70b and
      qwen3.6 hard-fail). ADR-0002 deviation DISCLOSED in-code: gpt-oss shares a family with the
      GPT/Codex build-time gate; the load-bearing separation (critic != system-under-test) holds,
      and no structured-output-capable third family is purchasable on this key today.
    - skeptic.ts: SKEPTIC_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS = 1_200, with the measurement recorded.
    - scripts/preflight-groq.mjs + npm run preflight{,:models,:groq} — the Gemini-only preflight was
      a HALF preflight over a two-provider system. preflight-models.mjs was also never wired to npm.
    - evals/cross-family-preflight.test.ts (new, 5 tests): pins the script<->code lockstep by READING
      THE SCRIPT'S TEXT (not recomputing through the same module — lesson #27) + pins pricing.
    - actionops-skeptic.test.ts: /llama-4/i pinned a BRAND and correctly went red; re-expressed as the
      durable invariants (no local default; never a Gemini model).
    - eslint/prettier: ignore .remember/** — agent-tooling scratch was linted as project source and
      turned `npm run verify` RED via --max-warnings=0.
    
    Evidence, first-hand 2026-07-27
    - npm run verify exit 0 — 916 unit / 34 golden / lint / contrast / build / secret-scan.
    - Skeptic calibration (gated, live): TPR 100% (7/7) / TNR 100% (10/10) — matches the historic
      llama-4-scout figures. Progression 40% -> 80% -> 100% as budget and spacing were corrected.
    - Live full-loop smoke: LIVE_AI / ACT / gatekeeper PASS / 2 playbooks / 5 drafts / $0.0221 / 38.1s.
    - Public `/` posture unchanged: $0 / keyless / frozen replay untouched.
    
    GATES OWED (not run here): acceptance-gate + Codex cross-model on this diff.
    Assessment: docs/claude/ASSESSMENT-2026-07-27.md · lessons L-1, L-2.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

