    fix(gate): discharge the acceptance-gate BLOCK — stale records + the judge, closed by measurement
    
    The gate BLOCKed `6104159` with two route-backs. Both were correct and material: it caught
    R-8 recurring INSIDE the commit that cites R-8 (class-grep run, not acted on to completion).
    
    Route-back 1 — three documents of record still asserted the decommissioned model, including
    `docs/Success_Criteria.md` (the file that defines the acceptance bar) and `docs/adr/0002` (the
    decision record this change DEVIATES from). "Recorded rather than silently reinterpreted" is not
    satisfied by recording it everywhere except the record.
    - ADR-0002: new `## Amendment (2026-07-27)` — forced model change, re-calibration, and the
      OpenAI-family overlap with the GPT/Codex build-time gate written into the ADR itself.
    - Success_Criteria.md + architecture.md: superseded with re-measured figures.
    - Widening the grep found two the gate did NOT name: architecture.md:81 still said
      `gemini-2.5-flash`; judge-calibration.test.ts:19 still stated the retired model's numbers as
      current (R-8's exact "just a comment" trap). Both fixed.
    - FULL triage table (every hit fix / N-A-with-reason) in the discharge record.
    
    Route-back 2 — the judge disclosure gap, CLOSED BY MEASUREMENT rather than a caveat. The shared
    constant had moved the judge's model too, to the candidate ADR-0002 had explicitly REJECTED
    (gpt-oss-120b 88.9%/0.889 vs llama-4-scout 100%/1.000).
    
    Measuring first exposed a SECOND live defect the gate had not seen: the judge harness fires all
    18 held-out items back-to-back with NO spacing, and judge.ts used the same unmeasured 4,000
    budget (779+4,000 = 4,779 of an 8,000 TPM window ~= 1 call/min). L-2 applied to the judge too.
    - JUDGE_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS = 1_200 (measured: in=779, out=165-252).
    - 15s TPM-derived spacing in evals/judge-calibration.test.ts.
    - Re-calibrated live: TPR 100% (9/9) / TNR 88.9% (8/9) / kappa 0.889 / errors 0/18, exit 0 —
      above the 0.83/0.83/0.60 bars and an EXACT reproduction of the ADR's five-week-old figure.
      Stated plainly: measurably weaker than the retired model, FORCED by the provider, not chosen.
    
    Advisories addressed
    - Negative control for the 5 new guard tests: mutate script default -> EXIT_MUTATED=1 (RED);
      revert -> EXIT_REVERTED=0 (GREEN). Exit codes captured directly (R-4).
    - preflight exit codes now evidenced: preflight:groq=0, preflight:models=0.
    - The `Requested 1752/1760` anomaly: the reservation claim is now SCOPED in-code as "evidenced,
      not proven universal", with the fix direction resting on the behavioural red->green instead.
    - preflight:groq is manual-only and thus half-closes its own root cause — DISCLOSED, not fixed:
      wiring it into `verify` would break the project's own P3.2 rule, and CI needs a GROQ_API_KEY
      secret (owner action).
    
    Deliberately NOT done: splitting the judge/Skeptic model constant. Single-sourcing prevents
    drift, which is the worse failure; the real defect was that the coupling was undocumented. It is
