   140	// The budget context a live call carries: how much has been spent so far this run, an
   141	// upper-bound estimate of THIS call's cost, and the cap. Threaded as a param (not a
   142	// global) so the guard is pure + DI-testable. Defaulted so a key-OFF/no-budget caller
   143	// is unaffected -- the guard only ever fires on a real live call that would breach.
   144	export type BudgetContext = {
   145	  spentUsd: number;
   146	  estimatedNextUsd: number;
   147	  capUsd?: number;
   148	};
   149	
   150	// The hard output-token ceiling on every live structured-output call. Bounding the output is
   151	// what makes the pre-call cost ESTIMATE a true upper bound (and thus the $5 hard-stop a real
   152	// guarantee, not a hope): without it, generateObject could emit far more than the estimated
   153	// envelope and overshoot the cap, which is asserted BEFORE the call. Sized with headroom for the
   154	// LARGEST agent output -- the Dispatcher's top-5 supplier drafts (subject + body + claims each):
   155	// too tight TRUNCATES the structured JSON mid-object and the parse throws. Kept in lockstep with
   156	// estimateLiveCallCostUsd's output envelope so the estimate can never under-price a real call.
   157	// EXPORTED (Codex P3 High): the Phase-3 Investigator loop's generateText caps its per-step output
