    62	
    63	## 3. Finding L-1 [CRITICAL] — the cross-family Skeptic model is decommissioned
    64	
    65	`GROQ_DEFAULT_MODEL = "meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct"` (`lib/agents/cross-family.ts:22`)
    66	is **not served by the Groq key**. Live listing returned 15 models; it is absent.
    67	
    68	**Blast radius** — one constant, two consumers (the single-sourcing is good; it means one fix):
    69	- `lib/agents/actionops/skeptic.ts:78` — the Phase-4 adversarial gate → **every live run holds**
    70	- `lib/evals/judge.ts:42` — the no-unsupported-claims judge → **the eval judge is down too**
    71	
    72	**Behaviour is correct-by-design, and that is the trap.** The Skeptic fails *closed*: a broken critic
    73	must not wave findings through, so it HOLDs and the packet degrades to `NO_ACTION`. The system is
    74	being safe. But from a user's seat the product silently produces nothing, and the fail-closed design
    75	means it will *never* raise an alarm about itself.
    76	
    77	**Why nothing caught it (the structural gap, not the model id):**
    78	1. `scripts/preflight-models.mjs` validates **Gemini only** — a half-preflight. Nothing validated the
    79	   cross-family provider.
    80	2. `evals/actionops-live-real.test.ts` **injects a stub ACCEPT Skeptic** (deliberately, to stop the
    81	   stochastic verdict flaking the Gemini assertions) — so the green gated live suite never exercises
    82	   the real critic.
    83	3. `grep` confirms **zero tests** reference `GROQ_DEFAULT_MODEL` or `groqAvailable`.
    84	4. The calibration suite that *would* have caught it is gated behind `RUN_LIVE_AI_TESTS` and is run
    85	   by hand.
    86	
    87	This is lesson **R-8 recurring on the other provider** — a duplicated/unguarded model default drifting
    88	out from under a validator. And it is exactly what `calibration-set-vs-real-finding` warns about:
    89	a perfect labelled score (TPR 100% / TNR 100%, measured 2026-06-22 on llama-4-scout) is not evidence
    90	the real artifact works today.
    91	
    92	**Replacement, verified live through the real `makeGroqGenerate` → `generateObject` path:**
    93	
    94	| Candidate | structured output | priced | latency |
    95	|---|---|---|---|
    96	| **`openai/gpt-oss-120b`** | **✅ works** | ✅ already in `GROQ_PRICING` | 893 ms |
    97	| `openai/gpt-oss-20b` | ✅ works | ✅ already in `GROQ_PRICING` | 514 ms |
    98	| `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` | ❌ `does not support response format json_schema` | ✗ | — |
    99	| `qwen/qwen3.6-27b` | ❌ `does not support response format json_schema` | ✗ | — |
   100	
   101	`gpt-oss-120b` is the pick: the strongest working candidate, genuinely cross-family from Gemini,
   102	and already priced so the cost ledger stays honest. Note only two of four models on the key support
   103	structured output at all — the schema constraint, not raw quality, is what narrows the field.
