   106	
   107	## 3b. Finding L-2 [HIGH] — the token budget was a THROUGHPUT knob, not a safety ceiling
   108	
   109	Repointing the model was not sufficient, and the way it failed is worth recording. After the swap
   110	the flagship smoke was perfect (ACT, gatekeeper PASS) — but the labelled calibration read
   111	**TPR 100% / TNR 40%**, with all six misses tagged `(error)`. The raw provider error:
   112	
   113	```
   114	429 Rate limit reached for `openai/gpt-oss-120b` ... tokens per minute (TPM):
   115	    Limit 8000, Used 5630, Requested 5421
   116	```
   117	
   118	**Groq reserves `input + max_completion_tokens` against the per-minute window, regardless of what
   119	the model actually emits.** The inherited `maxOutputTokens: 4_000` therefore reserved
   120	1,421 + 4,000 = 5,421 tokens for a call whose real output is ~370 (reasoning included) — about 11×
   121	over — so the second call in any minute was throttled. And because the Skeptic fails *closed*,
   122	every throttle became a HOLD that the harness scored as a false REJECT.
   123	
   124	Two counter-intuitive points:
   125	
   126	- **Raising the budget made it strictly worse.** At 16,000 the API returns `413 Request too large` —
   127	  a single call exceeding the entire minute's allowance. The fix was sizing *down* to 1,200
   128	  (>3× the measured need; reservation ~2,621; ~3 calls/min).
   129	- **The eval instrument carried the same stale assumption.** The harness's 4s inter-call spacing was
   130	  calibrated for llama-4-scout's ~30K TPM. Against an 8K ceiling it was measuring its own
   131	  throttling. TNR moved 40% → 80% → **100%** as the budget was right-sized and spacing went to 20s.
   132	
   133	Both gpt-oss sizes share the 8,000 ceiling, so switching model size buys no headroom. (The ceiling
   134	is readable off a deliberate `413`, which is rejected pre-inference and so costs nothing.)
   135	
   136	**Final calibration on the new model: TPR 100% (7/7) / TNR 100% (10/10)** — matching the historic
   137	llama-4-scout figures.
   138	
   139	### The judge — CLOSED by measurement (round 2, after the acceptance-gate BLOCK)
   140	
   141	The first pass disclosed only the *token-budget* consequence for `lib/evals/judge.ts`. The
   142	acceptance-gate correctly called that incomplete: the shared constant moved the **judge's model**
   143	too, and ADR-0002 had explicitly chosen llama-4-scout **over** gpt-oss-120b on the judge's own
   144	split (100%/1.000 vs 88.9%/0.889) — so the judge silently inherited the previously-*rejected*
   145	candidate.
   146	
   147	Rather than write a caveat, it was **measured**. Doing so exposed a second live defect the gate had
   148	not seen: the judge harness fires all 18 held-out items **back-to-back with no spacing**, and
   149	`judge.ts` used the same unmeasured 4,000 budget (779 + 4,000 = 4,779 of an 8,000 window ≈ one call
   150	per minute). **L-2 applied to the judge as well.** Fixed: `JUDGE_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS = 1_200`
   151	(measured in=779, out=165–252) plus 15s TPM-derived spacing.
   152	
   153	**Re-calibrated live, exit 0:** TPR 100% (9/9) · TNR 88.9% (8/9) · kappa 0.889 · errors 0/18 —
   154	above the enforced 0.83/0.83/0.60 bars, and an exact reproduction of the ADR's five-week-old figure.
   155	**Said plainly: measurably weaker than the retired model.** Forced by the provider, not chosen —
   156	only gpt-oss supports Groq `json_schema` on this key. Now recorded in ADR-0002 (as an amendment to
   157	the record it deviates from), `Success_Criteria.md`, `architecture.md`, the code, and lessons L-3.
   158	
   159	### Open follow-ons — recorded, deliberately NOT silently changed
   160	- **`npm run preflight:groq` is manual-only.** It is not in `verify` and not in CI. Since "run by
   161	  hand" was contributing cause #4 of L-1, the fix **half-closes its own root cause**. Wiring it into
   162	  `verify` would break the project's own P3.2 rule (no network smoke in the deterministic gate
   163	  chain), and CI needs a `GROQ_API_KEY` secret — an **owner action**. Stated rather than left silent.
   164	- **Judge/Skeptic model coupling** stays single-sourced (drift is the worse failure), but the cost is
   165	  now explicit in `judge.ts`: one repoint invalidates two calibrations. Splitting them is an
   166	  **owner-level architecture call**.
   167	- `maxRetries: 0` is deliberate (a Codex [High] finding: no un-ledgered retry may bill past the cap).
   168	  But a 429 is rejected pre-inference and costs nothing, so it currently degrades where it could
   169	  safely retry. **A `Retry-After`-aware single retry is the recommended hardening before the public
   170	  playground door opens** — under concurrent visitors an 8K TPM ceiling will throttle regularly.
   171	
   172	### Throughput reality for the Playground (new constraint, surfaced early)
   173	One Skeptic call per packet run reserves ~2,621 tokens of an 8,000/min budget → **~3 concurrent
   174	live runs per minute** before the cross-family critic starts degrading to HOLD. The planned per-IP
   175	limits and daily cap must be sized against *this*, not just against cost. Options: the retry above,
   176	a paid Groq tier, or an explicit queue.
   177	
