   **WHY:** This is not an external liveness alarm. It checks only ListModels membership plus a handwritten price set. A listed model can reject the actual schema mode, truncate, throttle, or fail completions while the script prints `OK`. More importantly, neither CI, `verify`, `verify:full`, deployment, nor startup invokes it. The same decommission therefore remains silent until a human manually runs the command.  
   **FIX:** Keep ListModels as a cheap first stage, but add a required scheduled/deployment health workflow with a secret that runs a minimal real structured-output call through each consumer’s actual schema and alerts outside the failing dependency. Do not mislabel a manual catalog check as operational liveness.

