   **WHY:** NWS payloads are compile-time casts, not runtime-validated. An HTTP-200 `{}`, error envelope, or contract-drift payload makes `data.features?.[0]` undefined and is reported as `SIG-NWS-CA-NONE`, `status:"LIVE"`, freshness zero—false calm rather than dependency failure. The live smoke then passes because it only trusts the app-authored `LIVE` label.  
   **FIX:** Runtime-parse the NWS response; require an explicitly present array before interpreting `[]` as “no alerts.” Malformed 200 responses must throw into the CACHED/failure path. Add `{}`, wrong-type, and malformed-feature negative tests.

